==English==

===Etymology===
From {{etyl|fr|en}} {{term|ressentiment|lang=fr}}, from {{term|ressentir|lang=fr}}

===Pronunciation===
* {{audio|en-us-resentment.ogg|Audio (US)}}

===Noun===
{{en-noun}}

# A feeling of [[anger]] or [[displeasure]] stemming from belief that others have engaged in [[wrongdoing]] or [[mistreatment]]; [[indignation]].
#* '''1812''', [[w:Jane Austen|Jane Austen]], ''Pride and Prejudice'', [[wikisource:Pride_and_Prejudice/Chapter_3|Chapter 3]]
#*: Amongst the most violent against him was Mrs. Bennet, whose dislike of his general behaviour was sharpened into particular '''resentment''' by his having slighted one of her daughters.

